{"name":"Purple Tanzanite","hex":"#835995","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"purple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour between red and blue; violet, though often closer to magenta.","Any non-spectral colour on the line of purples on a colour chromaticity diagram or a colour wheel between violet and red."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a purple hue.","Not predominantly red or blue, but having a mixture of Democrat and Republican support."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/purple"},{"term":"tanzanite","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A trichroic violet-blue variety of the mineral zoisite mined in Tanzania, used as a gemstone. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tanzanite"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tanzanite","blocks":[{"text":"Tanzanite is the blue and violet variety of the mineral zoisite. The color is caused by small amounts of vanadium. Tanzanite belongs to the epidote mineral group. Tanzanite is only found in Simanjiro District of Manyara Region in Tanzania, in a very small mining area approximately 7 km (4.3 mi) long and 2 km (1.2 mi) wide near the Mererani Hills."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Zo%C3%AFsite_%28Tanzanite%29.jpg/330px-Zo%C3%AFsite_%28Tanzanite%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tanzanite","wikidata":"Q429942"},{"title":"Purple","blocks":[{"text":"Purple is a color similar in appearance to violet light. In the RYB color model historically used in the arts, purple is a secondary color created by combining red and blue pigments. In the CMYK color model used in modern printing, purple is made by combining magenta pigment with cyan pigment, black pigment, or both. In the RGB color model used in computer and television screens, purple is created by mixing red and blue light in order to create colors that appear similar to violet light. According to color theory, purple is considered a cool color."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg/330px-Iris_sanguinea_cultivar%2C_Wakehurst_Place%2C_UK_-_Diliff.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purple","wikidata":"Q3257809"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Craft_work_on_tanzanite.jpg/500px-Craft_work_on_tanzanite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Craft_work_on_tanzanite.jpg/500px-Craft_work_on_tanzanite.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Craft work on tanzanite","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACraft_work_on_tanzanite.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Trichroic_Tanzanite_Crystal_-_violet_%26_burgundy.jpg/500px-Trichroic_Tanzanite_Crystal_-_violet_%26_burgundy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Trichroic_Tanzanite_Crystal_-_violet_%26_burgundy.jpg/500px-Trichroic_Tanzanite_Crystal_-_violet_%26_burgundy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Multicolored tanzanite crystal","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATrichroic_Tanzanite_Crystal_-_violet_%26_burgundy.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Trichroic_Tanzanite_Gem_-_blue%2C_violet_%26_purple.jpg/500px-Trichroic_Tanzanite_Gem_-_blue%2C_violet_%26_purple.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Trichroic_Tanzanite_Gem_-_blue%2C_violet_%26_purple.jpg/500px-Trichroic_Tanzani